{"title":"Addition","text":"<div class=\"mw-content-ltr mw-parser-output\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><p><b>Addition</b> is the mathematical <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Operation\" title=\"Operation\">operation</a> represented by the <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/7/c/77cf26be132ef93923e082ee4153b2cb0ef44a50.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$+$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"13\" height=\"12\" /> sign which combines two quantities. The result of addition is called a <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Sum\" title=\"Sum\">sum</a>. For example, the sum of 3 and 2 is 5 because <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/f/d/efd511c1545dc62444789b5e1f7ec0c0fec0b442.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$3+2=5$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"73\" height=\"14\" />.\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Notation\">Notation</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Addition&amp;action=edit&amp;section=1\" title=\"Edit section: Notation\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>The sum of two numbers <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/7/d/c7d457e388298246adb06c587bccd419ea67f7e8.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"10\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/1/3/8136a7ef6a03334a7246df9097e5bcc31ba33fd2.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$b$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"10\" height=\"14\" /> is denoted <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/d/d/add2609af1bb7632cc22b68fd49fdd94de06b327.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a+b$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"41\" height=\"16\" />, which is read \"a plus b.\" The two numbers being added together, or <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/7/d/c7d457e388298246adb06c587bccd419ea67f7e8.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"10\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/1/3/8136a7ef6a03334a7246df9097e5bcc31ba33fd2.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$b$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"10\" height=\"14\" />, are called addends. The sum of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/a/1/4a181ccdbf62e6e3754b1669e63095bc8902d1ed.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$f(a), f(a+1), f(a+2), f(a+3), \\cdots, f(b)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"331\" height=\"18\" />, where <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/b/2/bb2c93730dbb48558bb3c4738c956c4e8f816437.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$f$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"13\" height=\"18\" /> is a <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Function\" title=\"Function\">function</a>, is denoted <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/0/e/70e54ed34db6a7b8a3d786fd80d2de4a44e9918b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\sum_{i=a}^bf(i)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -20px\" width=\"58\" height=\"51\" />. (See also <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Sigma_notation\" title=\"Sigma notation\">Sigma notation</a>)\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Properties\">Properties</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Addition&amp;action=edit&amp;section=2\" title=\"Edit section: Properties\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<ul><li>Commutativity: The sum <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/d/d/add2609af1bb7632cc22b68fd49fdd94de06b327.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a+b$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"41\" height=\"16\" /> is equivalent to <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/2/b/62bdadf8cf9891bb42812ef0d8ebdfa6cc7feb9f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$b+a$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"39\" height=\"14\" />.</li>\n<li>Associativity: The sum <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/9/b/89bef36ae0cbb95ce2f5a4e3e57ab181c9e676ea.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$(a+b)+c$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"84\" height=\"18\" /> is equivalent to <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/d/b/0db16912814f17544c9bbde23b037cd36061bd03.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a+(b+c)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"82\" height=\"18\" />. This sum is usually denoted <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/e/b/6ebd1e0356cfe09c0d9b5459d6f1542657bb5891.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a+b+c$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"72\" height=\"16\" />.</li>\n<li>Distributivity: <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/5/e/e5ead56154d9869528c81c8b4e651c406b19d053.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a(b+c)=ab+ac$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"143\" height=\"18\" /></li>\n<li><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Closure\" title=\"Closure\">Closure</a>: If <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/7/d/c7d457e388298246adb06c587bccd419ea67f7e8.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"10\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/1/3/8136a7ef6a03334a7246df9097e5bcc31ba33fd2.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$b$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"10\" height=\"14\" /> are both elements of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/0/6/906fddead65545297c74bbc2ca83cd01f3f9ecc9.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\mathbb{R}$\" width=\"12\" height=\"12\" />, then <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/d/d/add2609af1bb7632cc22b68fd49fdd94de06b327.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a+b$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"41\" height=\"16\" /> is an element of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/0/6/906fddead65545297c74bbc2ca83cd01f3f9ecc9.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\mathbb{R}$\" width=\"12\" height=\"12\" />. This is also the case with <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/1/e/a1e6cd0e4103015efba12e0fc4291f012b467eaa.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\mathbb{N}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"15\" height=\"14\" />, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/4/0/d4023589a374e5b4a1bc6063d887aec205e0d3e0.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\mathbb{Z}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"14\" height=\"14\" />, and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/6/8/568df917149216103d9ba89ab22426e9449fb883.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\mathbb{C}$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"12\" height=\"13\" />.</li>\n<li>Identity: <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/2/2/622d458d9ed7ef284b7c54d55d07f85d111d6c1b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a+0=a$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"74\" height=\"14\" /> for any complex number <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/7/d/c7d457e388298246adb06c587bccd419ea67f7e8.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"10\" />.</li>\n<li>Inverse: The sum of a number and its <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Additive_inverse\" title=\"Additive inverse\">additive inverse</a>, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/e/c/4ecee2965fa810e59633da33d14c3e2ea3f6eb6c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a+(-a)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"68\" height=\"18\" />, is equal to <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=0\" title=\"0\">zero</a>.</li>\n<li>Equality: If <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/a/b/5abd2c942ae299fd26e18d0ca5d390a7ca4a8c34.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a=b$\" width=\"42\" height=\"12\" />, then <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/9/f/89f09782d7021f08289795397c440ef61b378814.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a+c=b+c$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"102\" height=\"14\" />.</li>\n<li>If <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/7/d/c7d457e388298246adb06c587bccd419ea67f7e8.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"10\" /> is real and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/1/3/8136a7ef6a03334a7246df9097e5bcc31ba33fd2.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$b$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"10\" height=\"14\" /> is positive, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/5/c/35c0de9a768a6acbbe18e944f19ba7dad18605e4.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a+b&gt;a$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"73\" height=\"14\" />.</li>\n<li>The sum of a number and its <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Complex_conjugate\" title=\"Complex conjugate\">Complex conjugate</a> is a real number.</li>\n<li><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/a/c/4acec6158ad706bb7f986be1a796eaf48a44d2d2.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a+(-b)=a-b$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"132\" height=\"18\" /> (See also <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Subtraction\" title=\"Subtraction\">Subtraction</a>)</li></ul>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"See_also\">See also</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Addition&amp;action=edit&amp;section=3\" title=\"Edit section: See also\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<ul><li><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Arithmetic\" title=\"Arithmetic\">Arithmetic</a></li>\n<li><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Number_theory\" title=\"Number theory\">Number theory</a></li>\n<li><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Subtraction\" title=\"Subtraction\">Subtraction</a></li>\n<li><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Hyperoperation&amp;action=edit&amp;redlink=1\" class=\"new\" title=\"Hyperoperation (page does not exist)\">Hyperoperation</a></li>\n<li><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Counting\" class=\"mw-redirect\" title=\"Counting\">Counting</a></li></ul>\n<p><i>This article is a stub.  Help us out by <span class=\"plainlinks\"><a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external text\" href=\"https://artofproblemsolving.com/wiki/index.php?title=Addition&amp;action=edit\">expanding it</a></span>.</i>\n</p>\n<!-- \nNewPP limit report\nCached time: 20261017203634\nCache expiry: 86400\nReduced expiry: false\nComplications: []\nCPU time usage: 0.023 seconds\nReal time usage: 0.034 seconds\nPreprocessor visited node count: 189/1000000\nPost‐expand include size: 265/2097152 bytes\nTemplate argument size: 0/2097152 bytes\nHighest expansion d